SUMMARY:TechTO Fast and Frugal Hackathon
DESCRIPTION:TechTO\n**This is a paid event. You must register and have a t
 icket to attend.** 🎟️ **Tickets are on Luma:** [Get your ticket here]
 (https://luma.com/hackathon-oct-17-2026?utm_source=meetup)\n\n**Eat. Code.
  Ship. Win 💲**\nWe’re back with another 12-hour build day on October 
 17 for builders\, dreamers\, and doers. We provide the food\, the mentors\
 , and the prize pool.\n\n**🎯 The Mission**\nBuild an AI agent that find
 s and books the best deal at a hotel in City X. Every agent runs the same 
 task at the same time. The fastest and cheapest booking wins.\n\n**📋 Th
 e Rules**\n\n* No ready-made agents\n* No browser automation tools\n* Agen
 ts must make a phone call and receive a receipt at a provided email addres
 s\n* Bring your friends\, public models\, and APIs\n\n**What’s Included*
 *\n\n* 🤝 Work alongside 100+ ambitious coders\, developers\, and design
 ers. You might just meet your next coding buddy.\n* 🏆 Compete for cash 
 prizes and cloud credits.\n* 👥 No team? We got you! We kick off the mor
 ning with a team-matching session to pair you with fellow builders.\n* ☕
  Complimentary coffee\, lunch\, dinner (pizza)\, and drinks are included w
 ith your ticket.\n\n**📝 Agenda**\n\n* **9:00 AM \\| Kickoff:** Doors op
 en\, check-in\, grab coffee\, and join your team.\n* **10:00 AM \\| Hackin
 g Begins:** 7 hours of uninterrupted building. Lunch at 1:00 PM.\n* **5:30
  PM \\| Demo & Pizza:** The Fast and Frugal Agent Bake-off.\n* **6:00 PM \
 \| Review Results**\n* **7:00 PM \\| Awards & Celebration:** Winners annou
 nced\, followed by a networking social until 9:00 PM.\n\n**👀 Meet the J
 udges**\n\n* **[Jatin Mehta](https://www.linkedin.com/in/jatinmehta1/)\, C
 o-founder of Speedy Labs:** a Y Combinator- and Google Ventures-backed AI 
 company helping enterprises optimize rebates\, deductions\, and trade spen
 d. With a background in AI research and engineering at Salesforce\, SAP\, 
 and HP\, he brings hands-on expertise in building and evaluating AI-driven
  products.\n* **[David Li](https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidy-li/)\, Co-fo
 under of Induction Labs:** a YC-backed AI research lab building foundation
  models that learn from video and computer-use data. He previously studied
  software engineering at the University of Waterloo and has ML research an
 d hackathon-winning experience.\n* **[Zeeshan Ahmed](https://www.linkedin.
 com/in/zeeshan1293/)\, Co-founder of Clara:** an AI-powered primary care a
 nd longevity practice. He previously led product design at Circle Medical 
 and worked on consumer experiences at Instagram and Careem.\n\n**🙌 Than
 ks to Our Sponsors:** ElevenLabs and Backboard.io\n\n*Tickets are non-tran
 sferable and non-refundable. By attending\, you acknowledge that photograp
 hy and video recording may take place at the event\, and you consent to re
 ceive newsletters and other communications from us.*
